+  "骰子判定：成功（点数 {roll}，需求 {rate}，勉强得手）。结果只是勉强够到了达标线，请描写行动勉强达成、略显吃力，或许留下一点小代价或遗憾，切勿渲染成轻松完胜。": "Dice decision: success (points {roll}, requirement {rate}, barely successful). The result is just barely reaching the goal line. Please describe the action as being barely achieved, a little difficult, and perhaps leaving a small cost or regret. Do not exaggerate it as an easy victory.",
+  "骰子判定：成功（点数 {roll}，需求 {rate}，险胜）。行动刚刚越过了达标线、优势微弱，请描写略带惊险、险中取胜的完成，过程不算从容但结果成立。": "Dice decision: success (point {roll}, requirement {rate}, narrow win). The action has just crossed the target line and the advantage is weak. Please describe a slightly thrilling and nearly successful completion. The process is not easy but the result is valid.",
+  "骰子判定：成功（点数 {roll}，需求 {rate}，顺利达成）。行动干净利落、顺理成章地完成，请描写过程平稳、结果扎实，不过于张扬也不拖泥带水。": "Dice decision: success (point {roll}, requirement {rate}, successfully achieved). The action was completed neatly and logically. Please describe the process as smooth and the results as solid, without being too showy or sloppy.",
+  "骰子判定：成功（点数 {roll}，需求 {rate}，漂亮完胜）。行动以出彩的姿态漂亮完成，请着重描写出色的发挥、加分的光彩，以及顺带带来的好处或余韵。": "Dice decision: success (point {roll}, requirement {rate}, beautiful victory). The action was beautifully completed with a brilliant attitude. Please focus on describing the outstanding performance, the brilliance of extra points, and the incidental benefits or aftertaste.",
+  "骰子判定：成功（点数 {roll}，需求 {rate}，势如破竹）。行动以碾压般的气势一举拿下，请着重描写压倒性的发挥、顺带的连锁好处，以及旁人的惊叹。": "Dice decision: success (point {roll}, requirement {rate}, overwhelming). The action was won in one fell swoop with a crushing momentum. Please focus on describing the overwhelming performance, the incidental chain benefits, and the amazement of others.",
+  "骰子判定：失败（点数 {roll}，未达需求 {rate}，差点成功）。几乎就要成了，请描写功亏一篑、与成功失之交臂的落差，那一线之差带来的懊恼与遗憾。": "Dice decision: Failure (points {roll}, did not meet the requirement {rate}, almost succeeded). It's almost done. Please describe the gap between falling short and missing out on success, and the annoyance and regret caused by that narrow gap.",
+  "骰子判定：失败（点数 {roll}，未达需求 {rate}，功亏一篑）。行动在半途受阻、差口气没能拿下，请描写临门一脚失手的不甘，以及这次失败留下的余地或伏笔。": "Dice decision: Failure (points {roll}, not up to the requirement {rate}, shortfall in effort). The action was blocked halfway and failed to win. Please describe your unwillingness to fail at the last moment and the room or foreshadowing left by this failure.",
+  "骰子判定：失败（点数 {roll}，未达需求 {rate}，事与愿违）。结果与预期相左，请描写行动受阻、实际走向偏离设想的局面，以及由此带来的纠葛或麻烦。": "Dice decision: Failure (points {roll}, did not meet the requirement {rate}, backfired). The result is contrary to expectations. Please describe the situation where the action is blocked, the actual direction deviates from the expectation, and the entanglements or troubles caused by it.",
+  "骰子判定：失败（点数 {roll}，需求 {rate}）。行动未能达成预期，请描写受挫的过程、由此产生的后续影响，并让角色对这一结果作出真实反应。": "Dice roll: Failure (Points {roll}, Requirement {rate}). If the action fails to meet expectations, please describe the frustration process, the subsequent impact, and let the character react realistically to the result.",
+  "骰子判定：失败（点数 {roll}，未达需求 {rate}，溃败）。行动明显失守、局面被动，请描写节节败退、落了下风的处境，以及随之扩大的损失。": "Dice decision: Failure (points {roll}, did not meet the requirement {rate}, defeated). The action is obviously lost and the situation is passive. Please describe the situation of losing ground and being at a disadvantage, as well as the ensuing losses.",
+  "骰子判定：失败（点数 {roll}，未达需求 {rate}，彻底落败）。行动一败涂地，请描写灰头土脸的惨况、随之而来的损失或难堪，让角色切实承受这次失败的代价。": "Dice decision: Failure (points {roll}, did not meet the requirement {rate}, complete defeat). If the operation fails miserably, describe the disgrace and subsequent loss or embarrassment so that the character truly feels the cost of the failure.",
+  "骰子判定：大成功（点数 {roll}）。行动以远超预期的完美方式达成，请着重描写这一惊艳的结果——角色出色的发挥、他人的赞叹，以及随之而来的额外好处。": "Dice roll: Big success (points {roll}). The action was accomplished in a way that was far better than expected. Focus on the amazing result—the role played well, the admiration of others, and the additional benefits that followed.",
+  "骰子判定：大失败（点数 {roll}）。行动不仅失败，还引发了严重的事故或连锁反应，请描写灾难性的后果，并让角色为这一失误付出实实在在的代价。": "Dice roll: Big fail (points {roll}). The action not only failed, but also caused a serious accident or chain reaction. Please describe the catastrophic consequences and make the character pay a real price for this mistake.",
+  "收到，开始按问题梳理场景与方向。\\n\\n<thinking>\\n": "After receiving it, I started sorting out the scenarios and directions according to the questions. \\n\\n<thinking>\\n",
+  "收到，开始处理润色任务：先理解原文，再自检人称、字数、忠实度。\\n\\n<thinking>\\n": "After receiving it, start the polishing task: first understand the original text, and then self-check the person, Character count, and fidelity. \\n\\n<thinking>\\n",
+  "输出必须以 <thinking> 标签开头：直接进入逐条分析与自检，不要先写任何致意、过渡或客套话；分析与自检完成后再输出 <options>。": "The output must start with the <thinking> tag: directly enter the item-by-item analysis and self-inspection, do not write any greetings, transitions or polite words first; output <options> after the analysis and self-inspection are completed.",
+  "输出必须以 <thinking> 标签开头，直接进入润色前的处理与自检（先理解原文，再检查人称、字数、忠实度），不要先写任何致意或过渡语；全部检查完成后再输出 <options>。": "The output must start with the <thinking> tag, and go directly to the processing and self-checking before polishing (understand the original text first, and then check the pronoun, Character count, and fidelity). Do not write any greetings or transitional words first; output <options> after all checks are completed.",
+  "思维链起手": "Start thinking chain",
+  "【认知边界：非全知约束】\n以下规则高于本批候选的一切信息来源约束：\n\n1. 信息分层：你读到的全部内容里，只有两类能被候选直接依赖——①此刻可感知：当前场景里该主体眼前能看到、耳边能听到、能碰到、能闻到的具体细节（道具、在场者状态与台词、空间特征）；②该主体已知：角色设定与经历中明确属于该主体早已知道的事（自己的名字、与在场者既有关系、亲历过的往事）。其余一律视为该主体此刻不知道——包括世界书/背景里只有读者能看到的信息（他人秘密计划、远方发生的事、尚未公开的真相、角色未被告知的身份）。\n\n2. 禁止越界：候选不得让该主体直接使用它看不到、不知道的信息作为依据；不得对视线外/未被当面告知的事物行动（不许「去后门堵住他」这类）。若确要推动一条隐藏线索，必须通过此刻可见的钩子触发——看见异样、听见动静、被当面告知、从某个细节察觉——并写成「因注意到…/因怀疑…而行动」。\n\n3. 逐条核查：每条候选落地前，在 <thinking> 里自问——这条依赖的信息，是该主体此刻能感知的、还是早已知道的？若依赖了只有读者能看到的信息，把它改成由可感知钩子触发，或直接删除该候选。": "【Cognitive boundaries: non-omniscient constraints】\nThe following rules are higher than all information source constraints for this batch of candidates:\n\n1. Information layering: Of all the content you read, there are only two categories that candidates can directly rely on - ① Perceivable at the moment: specific details that the subject can see, hear, touch, and smell in the current scene (props, status and lines of the participants, spatial features); ② Known by the subject: things in the character setting and experience that the subject already knows (his name, existing relationships with the people present, and past events he has experienced). Everything else is considered unknown to the subject at the moment - including information in the World Info/background that only the reader can see (others' secret plans, things happening in the distance, truths that have not yet been revealed, characters' identities that have not been revealed).\n\n2. No cross-border crossing: the candidate must not allow the subject to directly use information that it cannot see or know as a basis; it must not act on things that are out of sight/that have not been informed in person (no \"blocking him at the back door\" or the like). If you really want to push forward a hidden clue, it must be triggered through the hook that is visible at the moment - seeing something strange, hearing a movement, being told face to face, noticing from a certain detail - and write \"because of noticing.../acting because of suspicion...\".\n\n3. Verification one by one: Before each candidate is implemented, ask yourself in <thinking> - Is this dependent information something the subject can perceive at the moment, or is it already known? If you rely on information that only readers can see, change it to be triggered by a perceptible hook, or delete the candidate directly.",
+  "每条候选落在当前场景一个具体可见的细节上（道具、状态、台词、空间特征），不凭空引入新设定，也不复述已发生的事。\n\n候选独立于正文（本身不算已发生）；只写所选主体自身的行动与台词，不替演它落地后其他各方的反应；只用该主体此刻能知道的信息，涉及未公开真相时写成\"因怀疑/听说而行动\"。需要言语的候选，话必须说出来：用『……』直接引语给出完整可朗读的台词，整句可直接发进正文；禁止只描述说话动作不给原话——\"询问她是否知道地址\"\"淡然问她记不记得\"这类转述是错误示范，应写成『珞花现在住哪儿？』『还记得被狗追三条街的事吗？』；凡选项里含说/问/告诉的意图，就必须配一句『……』原话。纯动作/观察/场景演化的候选不受此限，不必硬塞台词。整批候选在主体、切入点、风险上拉开差距——至少一条往前推进实质一步（带来新信息、新事件或关系变化），可含 0-1 条\"不行动/改话题\"；每条标题里标注风险档位（保守/平衡/大胆，见输出格式）与需求值（见输出格式），档位整批尽量错开、需求值随难度区分。\n\n输出格式是硬约束：全部候选输出成 <options> 内的 JSON 数组，数组用 [ ] 包裹、每个候选是一个对象、元素间用逗号分隔，对象形如 {\"title\":\"标题|档位|需求值\",\"content\":\"正文\"}。title 是简洁行动标题，可用竖线追加标注：第一条竖线后标注 保守/平衡/大胆 三档之一，按该选项风险与力度判断；第二条竖线后为 0-100 的需求值整数，代表达成该选项所需的骰子点数下限（掷出 ≥ 需求值才算成功、点数越大越好）——行动越难、成功把握越低，标得越高；拿不准档位或需求值就省略对应竖线段，不许乱标。content 是候选正文字符串，每条 {{min_chars}}-{{max_chars}} 字；content 用单个 JSON 字符串表示、不要在其中换行，可含任意字符（包括 []、【】），一切结构只由外层 JSON 承担，不要用括号在正文里做任何标记。只许出现 <thinking> 与 <options> 两个标签，不输出 {{xxx}} 占位符、不造额外标签，</options> 之后一字不写。人称：严格按 {{option_person}} 写，忽略上方聊天记录正文自己的人称选择。": "Each candidate falls on a specific visible detail of the current scene (props, status, lines, spatial features), without introducing new settings out of thin air, nor retelling what has happened.\n\nThe candidate is independent of the main text (it does not count as having happened); only the selected subject's own actions and lines are written, and the reactions of other parties after it is not acted out; only the information that the subject can know at the moment is used, and when the undisclosed truth is involved, write \"action due to suspicion/hearing\". For candidates who need words, the words must be spoken: Use \"...\" direct quotation to give a complete readable line, and the entire sentence can be sent directly into the text; it is prohibited to only describe the speaking action without giving the original words - \"Ask her if she knows the address\", \"Ask her calmly if she remembers\". Such paraphrases are wrong examples and should be written as \"Where does Luohua live now?\" \"Do you still remember the time when the dog chased you three streets?\" \"; If the option contains the intention of saying/asking/telling, it must be accompanied by the original sentence \"...\". Candidates who are pure action/observation/scenario evolution are not subject to this restriction and do not have to cram in lines. The entire batch of candidates should widen the gap in terms of subjects, entry points, and risks - at least one of them will take a substantial step forward (bringing new information, new events, or changes in relationships), and can include 0-1 \"no action/change of topic\"; each title is marked with the risk level (conservative/balanced/bold, see the output format) and the demand value (see the output format). The gears should be staggered throughout the batch as much as possible, and the demand value is differentiated according to the difficulty.\n\nThe output format is a hard constraint: all candidates are output into an JSON array within <options>. The array is wrapped with [ ], each candidate is an object, and the elements are separated by commas. The object is in the shape of {\"title\":\"Title|Scale|Required Value\",\"content\":\"Text\"}. title is a concise action title, and can be additionally marked with vertical lines: one of the three levels of conservative/balanced/bold is marked after the first vertical line, judged according to the risk and intensity of the option; after the second vertical line is the integer demand value of 0-100, which represents the lower limit of the dice points required to achieve this option (throw ≥ The required value is required to be considered a success (the bigger the points, the better) - the more difficult the action and the lower the probability of success, the higher the mark; if you are not sure about the gear or the required value, omit the corresponding vertical line segment and do not mark randomly. content is a candidate text string, each {{min_chars}}-{{max_chars}} character; content is ​​represented by a single JSON string, do not break lines in it, and can contain any characters (including [], 【】). All structures are only borne by the outer JSON. Do not use parentheses to make any marks in the text. Only two labels, <thinking> and <options>, are allowed to appear. The {{xxx}} placeholder is not output, no additional labels are created, and no word is written after </options>. Person: Strictly write as {{option_person}}, ignore your own person choice in the chat record text above.",
+  "正式输出前，把思考写出来，全部裹在 <thinking> 标签里。逐条作答，每一条一两句即可：\n1. 现在是什么场景？——地点、在场者、最新一条动作/台词各是什么，场景停在哪个留白上；从最近一两层正文挑 2-3 个能直接落进候选的细节。\n2. 本轮素材（固定+候选条目）分别指向什么方向？由谁来做、做到什么程度、会带来什么变化；选哪几个组合进这批候选。\n3. 这批候选的差异与合规：有没有重复的，或只是\"叹气/沉默/转身离开/凝视\"这类空动作？需要言语的候选是否都把话落成了『……』原话、而不是\"询问\"\"问道\"这类转述？主体、切入点、风险是否拉开差距？风险档位（保守/平衡/大胆）是否标对、整批错开？需求值（0-100 的整数）是否按难度给出、与档位风险趋同（越难越高）？核对：恰好 {{count}} 条，格式与字数按系统消息的格式规则，人称按 {{option_person}}。核对无误即进入 <options>。": "Before formal output, write down your thoughts and wrap them all in the <thinking> tag. Answer each item one by one, one or two sentences for each:\n1. What is the scene now? ——The location, the people present, what is the latest action/line, and which blank space the scene stops on; pick 2-3 details that can directly fall into the candidate list from the last one or two layers of text.\n2. In what direction do the materials of this round (fixed + candidate entries) point? Who will do it, to what extent, and what changes will be brought about; which combinations will be selected into this batch of candidates.\n3. Differences and compliance of this batch of candidates: Are there any repetitions, or just empty actions such as \"sigh/silence/turn away/stare\"? Do the candidates who need words use the original words of \"...\" instead of paraphrases such as \"asking\" or \"asking\"? Are the subjects, entry points, and risks widening the gap? Are the risk levels (conservative/balanced/bold) correctly marked and staggered across batches? Are the demand values ​​(integers from 0-100) given in order of difficulty, converging with the risk of the gear (the harder, the higher)? Verification: Exactly {{count}}, the format and Character count follow the system message format rules, and the person name is {{option_person}}. Once verified, enter <options>.",
